    • Each run is represented as character + decimal count.
    • Empty input produces an empty encoding.
4. Algorithm
1. Read text.
2. Track the current character and run length.
3. When a character changes, append the prior run.
4. Append the final run and compare lengths.
5. Flowchart

Flowchart represented as a linear decision/process diagram for clear rendering in Word.
Start → Enter a string → Initialize the encoded string → Read the characters one by one → Count consecutive repeated characters → Append each character followed by its run count → Repeat until all characters are processed → Calculate the original string length → Calculate the encoded string length → Compare both lengths → Display the original string, encoded string, and their lengths → Stop.

